# Handoff protocol

Before coding, read:
1. `CURSOR_HANDOFF.md` — builder role, loop, anti-scope
2. `STATUS.md` — current gate, debt, next feature
3. `CONTEXT.md` — locked decisions and constraints
4. `ARCHITECTURE.md` — honest built vs partial inventory
5. `PARKING_LOT.md` — do not build from here

After shipping: update `STATUS.md`, append `CHANGELOG_DMS.md`, run `pytest -q`, then `python scripts/handoff.py --write`.
After gate PASS/FAIL: refresh `CLAUDE_HANDOFF.md` via `--write`.

## Git push (required)

After any ship, gate update, or handoff refresh that changes tracked files:

1. `git status` — stage only intentional changes (never `key.md`, `env.local`, `.next/`, secrets).
2. Commit with a concise message (why, not file list).
3. **`git push origin HEAD`** — always push; do not leave shipped work local-only.

If push fails (auth, conflict), report the error and fix before ending the session.

## Subagents

| Need | Action |
|------|--------|
| Ship F/V feature (sequential) | `Use dms-subagent-dispatch` |
| Read-only codebase research | Task `explore` — parallel OK |
| Gate verification | `Use dms-claude-gate` — read-only |
| Multi-module audit | Parallel `explore` subagents, then one synthesis |

Never parallelize dependent feature builds (F1→F7→V0→V1).

## Claude handoff

Run `python scripts/handoff.py --claude` or paste `CLAUDE_HANDOFF.md` into new Claude chat.

## Cursor handoff

Run `python scripts/handoff.py --cursor` or read `CURSOR_HANDOFF.md` at session start.

## Ponytail

Use YAGNI / stdlib-first (`PONYTAIL_DEFAULT_MODE=full`). Review for over-engineering before merge.

